  "body": "## Result and scope\n\nRetained-total column 7 of the pinned PR1062 R439 word needs exactly **five scalar scatter ADDs** even when its taps may occur at every target and every cut of either of two fixed undo orders: the literal 306 gates, or the 303 deferred gates after PR2115's known `{31,51,52}` split.\n\nThe known 94-ADD split already uses five taps for this column. This contribution rules out improving that column to four taps in these two interleaving classes; **no new kappa or supplier adoption is claimed**. PR2279 proves the all-ideal split optimum and explicitly excludes scatter interleavings. This result adds distinct evidence in that excluded class; it does not prove a global interleaving optimum or cover arbitrary commuting orders, other columns, mixed copied totals, or new target gates.\n\n## Exact evidence\n\n- Complete suffix dictionaries: 415 / 412 distinct 111-bit responses over all 34,077 / 33,744 tap locations.\n- Complete sums of at most two responses: 83,624 / 82,435 values. Their translated intersections are empty, excluding every sum of at most four taps. Five explicit taps attain the required response.\n- A separately written checker reconstructs coefficients with forward set-valued matrix rows instead of backward columns, and executes both witnesses forwards. The two-plus-two coverage lemma is shared; this is algorithmic independence, not independent human review.\n- Full local witness records pass all 661 dirty input columns in both directions, exact COPY/ERASE checks, ordered frame MOVEs, paid profiles and positive majorants. The ideal-order witness matches the known 11,067 total ADDs, with nine rank-seven copies, nine erasures, one temporary, rank mass 5,129 and 95/181 guard bits. Every undo gate remains charged.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/r439-interleaved-scatter-seed16\n```\n\nExpected final marker: `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=negative-result`.\n\nThe registered CPython 3.12.13 replay passed locally: normal and optimized primary checks, independent reconstruction, 12 primary / 6 independent controls, and actual-entry-point Git-free read-only relocation and corruption checks. `git diff --cached --check` passes. No selected cold replay or hosted CI pass is claimed.\n\nNative phase/parser admission of undo gates inside a live COPY, whole-call hosting, all-size/compiler realization, physical precision/tapes and outer assembly remain open or inherited. The finite coefficient result does not establish the full multiplication theorem.\n\n## Provenance and credit\n\nBase: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, priority revision 4. OS-random assignment seed **16**, bit-supplier track, selects column `16 mod 9 = 7`. The local claim, three candidates, stopping rule and completed coverage are in `TASK.json`; no pinned coordination issue existed. All changes are confined to one new research package. The selected frontier and `upstream/` are unchanged.\n\nExact live inputs and document pins are in `SOURCES.json`. Credit Sagar Thakrar's PR1062/PR2115 (`b56dceffad83c88e8ad39ffd82a1bdd55c4130da`), Charles Bethin's PR2279 (`81fed971e2269b62eae2ee8e3b6bda394930992c`), Gareth Davidson's PR915 basis, and the helper-star/B-circuit/frame/PR589/PR555/interface/exporter lineage retained in README. Both predecessor heads were refreshed before submission.\n\nPrepared by Sricharan Vagvala (@theon199) with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in mathematics, implementation, verification and writing; parent-only, no subagents or independent human review. Apache-2.0.\n\nFinal overlap refresh at 2026-10-15T06:20:01.702351+00:00 covered 564 open PRs and 1078 Discussion records, complete pagination and no warnings. The only external match was PR2279, whose explicitly excluded interleaving class is addressed here. The local claim is updated DONE with the public branch artifact link.\n",
